.TH LLMC++ 1 "" "llmcpp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llmc++ \- compile C++ with LLM-generated function bodies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llmc++
.RI [ options ] " source ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
llmc++ is a Clang-based C++ compiler driver. Functions and lambdas marked
with __llm__ have their bodies generated from the instructions inside their
braces. Generated bodies are checked by the compiler before acceptance.
Other compiler and linker options are forwarded to Clang.
.PP
The modifier accepts an optional parenthesized list of per-function options.
Generation requires a configured backend unless accepted bodies are cached.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-fllm
Accepted for compatibility. Generation is already enabled.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-backend= backend
Select anthropic, openai, codex, or claude, overriding LLMCPP_BACKEND.
Generation requires an explicit backend unless a custom agent is supplied.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-agent= command
Run an external JSON-RPC agent instead of selecting a backend.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-model= id
Select the default model, overriding LLMCPP_MODEL.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-system\-prompt= file
Replace the built-in system prompt with a UTF-8 file.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-append\-system\-prompt= file
Append a UTF-8 file to the system prompt. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-agent\-config= file
Pass a JSON configuration object to an external agent. Selects the Python
adapter instead of a native API client.
.TP
.B \-fllm\-offline
Use cached bodies only. Do not contact an agent.
.TP
.B \-fllm\-regenerate
Ignore cached bodies and generate fresh ones.
.TP
.B \-fllm\-no\-cache
Disable cache reads and writes.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-cache\-dir= directory
Choose the cache directory. The default is .llmcache beside the source file.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-hash\-abbrev= count
Set the minimum hash length in generated comments and cache filenames.
Default: 7. Range: 1 through 64. Ambiguous prefixes grow automatically.
Full SHA-256 hashes remain in cache metadata for validation.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-max\-attempts= count
Limit rejected submissions per body. Default: 4.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-max\-tool\-calls= count
Limit compiler tool calls per body. Default: 60.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-timeout= seconds
Set the generation deadline per body. Default: 600.
All numeric limits must be positive integers.
.TP
.B \-fllm\-dump
Print accepted generated bodies.
.TP
.B \-fllm\-dump\-context
Print task and compiler context without contacting an agent.
.TP
.B \-fllm\-verbose
Print generation progress, agent tool calls, and short results.
.TP
.BI \-fllm\-transcript= file
Append generation, tool, and outcome events to a JSONL transcript.
.TP
.B \-\-llm
Write rewritten source and stop instead of compiling. Output defaults to
<name>.llm.cpp, or <name>.llm.ii with \-E. Use \-o to select an output file.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
An output filename ending in .cpp, .cc, or .cxx implies \-\-llm.
Other output filenames retain normal compiler behavior unless \-\-llm is passed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LLMCPP_BACKEND
Select anthropic, openai, codex, or claude. Overridden by \-fllm\-backend.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_AGENT
External agent command, overridden by \-fllm\-agent.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_MODEL
Default model, overridden by \-fllm\-model and per-function model options.
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY
Credentials for the corresponding API backend.
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL ", " OPENAI_BASE_URL
Override the corresponding API endpoint.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_EFFORT
Reasoning effort for Codex and Claude Code. Default: medium.
.TP
.BR LLMCPP_CODEX ", " LLMCPP_CLAUDE
CLI executable names or paths. Defaults: codex and claude.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_VERBOSE
Enable Python adapter diagnostics when nonempty.
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.B __llm__
Generate using driver defaults. __llm__() has the same effect.
.TP
.B model("id")
Override the model for one function.
.TP
.B backend("name")
Override the backend for one function: anthropic, openai, codex, or claude.
A configured custom agent still takes precedence over native API transports.
.TP
.B no_cache
Disable cache reads and writes for one function.
.TP
.B offline
Require a cached body for one function and fail on a cache miss without contacting
an agent. Enable cache reads even with \-fllm\-no\-cache and ignore
\-fllm\-regenerate. Cannot be combined with no_cache.
.TP
.B cache("salt")
Enable caching and add a nonempty salt to the cache key, not a filename.
Cannot be combined with no_cache.
.TP
.B key("hash")
Use an explicit cache identity of 7 to 64 hexadecimal characters, or an
unambiguous prefix of an existing identity. Reuse cached code despite changed
generation inputs. A miss generates and saves under this key. Ambiguous prefixes
are errors. Enable caching; cannot be combined with no_cache.
.TP
.B max_attempts(count)
Override the rejected-submission limit with a positive integer literal.
.TP
.B timeout(seconds)
Override the generation deadline with a positive integer literal.
.PP
Separate options with commas inside __llm__(...). Per-function options
override driver defaults but cannot enable generation in offline mode.
.SH MACROS
.B __LLMCPP__
is defined as 1 during compilation and preprocessing.
Use #ifdef __LLMCPP__ to distinguish this compiler from other compilers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
LLMCPP_BACKEND=codex llmc++ main.cpp \-o main
llmc++ \-fllm\-offline main.cpp \-o main
llmc++ \-\-llm main.cpp
llmc++ \-fllm\-dump\-context main.cpp
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A nonzero status indicates a configuration,
generation, compilation, or linking failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llmcpp-agent (1),
.BR clang (1)
